From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] shared/netutils/dhcpserver: find the message type anywhere in
 the options.

The server read the DHCP message type from the first option. dhcpcd puts
the requested address first in a REQUEST, so the server ignored it: dhcpcd
got an OFFER and never an ACK, and fell back to a link-local address.
Windows and most other clients put the type first, which hid it. The type
is now looked up like every other option.
---
 shared/netutils/dhcpserver.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/shared/netutils/dhcpserver.c b/shared/netutils/dhcpserver.c
--- a/shared/netutils/dhcpserver.c
+++ b/shared/netutils/dhcpserver.c
@@ -208,7 +208,14 @@
     uint8_t *opt = (uint8_t *)&dhcp_msg.options;
     opt += 4; // assume magic cookie: 99, 130, 83, 99
 
-    switch (opt[2]) {
+    // The message type can be any option, not only the first: dhcpcd puts
+    // the requested address ahead of it in a REQUEST.
+    uint8_t *msg_type = opt_find(opt, DHCP_OPT_MSG_TYPE);
+    if (msg_type == NULL) {
+        goto ignore_request;
+    }
+
+    switch (msg_type[2]) {
         case DHCPDISCOVER: {
             int yi = DHCPS_MAX_IP;
             for (int i = 0; i < DHCPS_MAX_IP; ++i) {
-- 
2.43.0

